      "note": "Adapted independent test expectations and interface/seam vocabulary with scoped architecture exploration; other upstream workflow changes are not imported."
    },
    "matt-quality": {
      "repository": "mattpocock/skills",
      "revision": "4ae2317ddb22b046e26455e4f9c9b3aaaf62212d",
      "note": "Adapted the standards and spec review axes with the Fowler smell baseline as judgement calls, extended with a correctness lens; and the diagnosing-bugs red loop criteria, ranked hypotheses and forced-mutation diff check."
    },
    "matt-testing": {
      "repository": "mattpocock/skills",
      "revision": "4ae2317ddb22b046e26455e4f9c9b3aaaf62212d",
      "note": "Adapted the seam-first test plan, where each kept test states what it catches and misses; Grillmester states the plan and asks only when the seam or the kept tests are an unsettled material choice."
    },
    "matt-grilling": {
      "repository": "mattpocock/skills",
      "revision": "4ae2317ddb22b046e26455e4f9c9b3aaaf62212d",
      "note": "Adapted round-based grilling over the decision frontier, thin grill-me and grill-with-docs entries, and the GLOSSARY.md convention with CONTEXT.md as a fallback; documentation writes stay behind an explicit request or acceptance."
    },
    "matt-additions": {
      "repository": "mattpocock/skills",
      "revision": "4ae2317ddb22b046e26455e4f9c9b3aaaf62212d",
      "note": "Adapted two user-invoked skills, retro as agent-retro and wait-what, and the context-pointer rules for descriptions from writing-for-agents in create-a-skill's principles."
    },
    "matt-delivery": {
      "repository": "mattpocock/skills",
      "revision": "4ae2317ddb22b046e26455e4f9c9b3aaaf62212d",
      "note": "Adapted the pull-request body shape (a summary with the smallest useful visual, before-and-after evidence, and the merge danger as a one-way or two-way door with its blast radius) as the default when a repository has no template, and suggested skills in a handoff; the menu of summary visuals that upstream credits to Humanlayer's show-me is not reproduced."
    },
    "nav-observability": {
      "repository": "navikt/copilot",
      "revision": "ce9abd567a89eb72f1b8f95447435fd16fe805d3",
      "note": "Adapted trace representativeness guidance from observability-debugging; endpoint and command recipes are not imported. Local data-access rules were also checked against Nav's published guidelines and observability workflow at this revision."
    },
    "nav-tokenx": {
      "repository": "navikt/copilot",
      "revision": "2145f233dd35a62b5674d5f526bcf9417e741f03",
      "note": "Adapted four points from tokenx-auth: a Texas failure surfaces as 5xx, not 401; one skip_cache retry after an access-policy change; client_id checks when authorizing per calling app; and both acr forms. Code and request examples are not imported. The other Texas corrections were checked against the Nais documentation."
    }
